# Who owns and moderates each part of the wiki.
#
# This is the wiki's permission model, and it is GitHub's own rather than
# something the site invents. Every edit made through xrwiki.toastconcern.dev
# arrives as a commit or a pull request, so naming a person here is what makes
# them the moderator of a page: GitHub requests their review automatically on
# any pull request touching a path they own, and the site prints them under
# "Maintainers" at the top of every page they cover.
#
# Rules are read top to bottom and THE LAST MATCHING RULE WINS, so the general
# rule goes first and the specific ones under it.
#
# Two things to know:
#   - An owner must have write access to this repository. Add them under
#     Settings -> Collaborators and teams first, or the rule is ignored.
#   - For a review to be *required* rather than merely requested, turn on
#     Settings -> Branches -> branch protection for `main` and tick
#     "Require review from Code Owners".

# ---------- owners of the whole wiki ----------

*                                   @Toastconcern

# ---------- moderators, by section ----------
#
# Uncomment a line and add the handles of whoever looks after that part.
# Everything not listed falls back to the owners above.

# docs/meta/montereyGuides/          @Toastconcern
# docs/meta/roottweaks/              @Toastconcern
# docs/pico/                         @Toastconcern
# docs/valve/                        @Toastconcern

# ---------- the site itself ----------
#
# Structure and code, as opposed to the guides: a change here affects every
# page, so it stays with the owners no matter who moderates a section.

/docs/_sidebar.md                    @Toastconcern
/docs/index.html                     @Toastconcern
/docs/style.css                      @Toastconcern
/docs/wiki.css                       @Toastconcern
/docs/code.js                        @Toastconcern
/docs/wiki.js                        @Toastconcern
/.github/                            @Toastconcern
